course: dictionary
lesson: 578
title: Autism: a different brain
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Autism is a difference in how a person's brain works. It is lifelong, so it does not go away, and it is not an illness you can catch. «Autism means a brain that works differently.» Every autistic person is different from every other autistic person.
explain: Autism can affect how a person communicates, how they make sense of the world and how they deal with other people. «Autistic people may find unwritten playground rules confusing, and a patient buddy can help.» Unwritten means nobody has written the rule down, so you have to learn it by watching and asking.
explain: Many autistic people find noise, bright light or busy places hard. «Too much noise or light can cause a meltdown, which is not naughtiness.» A meltdown is when someone becomes overwhelmed, so the kind response is a quiet space and patience, not telling them off.
explain: Autism is not anybody's fault. Some disabilities are easy to see, like «a wheelchair, a white cane», and some are invisible, like «diabetes, a heart problem, autism or ADHD». You cannot always tell by looking, so always be kind.
fact: Autism is a lifelong difference in how a person's brain works.
fact: Autistic people are all different, and they may have strong special interests and talents.
fact: Autism is not an illness to catch and not anybody's fault.
fact: Autistic people may like routines and may find changes hard, so a warning before a change can help.
fact: Phrases you may hear are «autism spectrum» and «on the spectrum», which mean that autism affects people in many different ways.
exercise: What is autism? | A kind of food allergy | An illness you can catch from other people | A sort of bad behaviour | *A lifelong difference in how the brain works
exercise: Some autistic people find noise and busy places hard. What can help them? | *A quiet space and a warning before changes | Being told to stop being silly | Making more noise to join in | Being ignored completely
exercise: What does lifelong mean? | Only when it is cold | For one week only | *For the whole of a person's life | Only in school
test: Can you catch autism from another child? | Yes, from the playground | Yes, if you sit too close | Only in winter | *No, it is a difference in how the brain works
test: What is a meltdown? | A kind of playground rule | *When someone is overwhelmed, and it is not naughtiness | Shouting on purpose to be rude | A game played at the end of school
exam: A classmate who is autistic is upset by the noise in the hall. What is the kindest response? | Laugh so they relax | Shout louder so they can hear you | Tell them to stop being silly | *Offer a quiet space and speak calmly
